---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Service — WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com';
const description =
  'Terms of service for WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com. By using our free quitclaim deed generator, you agree to these terms.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: title,
  url: 'https://whatisaquitclaimdeed.com/terms-of-service/',
  description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/terms-of-service/">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Terms of Service</span>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="page-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: July 2026</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Please read these Terms of Service ("Terms") carefully before using WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com
      (the "Site"). By accessing or using the Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do
      not agree to these Terms, please do not use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Description of Service</h2>
    <p>
      WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com provides a free online tool for generating quitclaim deed documents
      based on information you provide. The Site also provides educational information about quitclaim
      deeds and related real estate topics.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Not Legal Advice</h2>
    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>
        <strong>WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice.</strong>
        The information and documents provided by this Site are for informational and educational
        purposes only and do not constitute legal advice. Use of this Site does not create an
        attorney-client relationship between you and WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com or any of its
        operators.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for ensuring that any document generated through this Site is appropriate
        for your specific situation, complies with applicable law, and has been reviewed by a
        licensed attorney if necessary. We strongly encourage you to consult a licensed real estate
        attorney before executing any deed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>3. User Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>By using the Site, you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accurate and complete information when using our deed generator</li>
      <li>Use the Site only for lawful purposes</li>
      <li>Not use the Site to generate documents intended to defraud or harm any person</li>
      <li>Not attempt to reverse-engineer, copy, or reproduce any part of the Site</li>
      <li>Not use automated means to access or scrape the Site without our written permission</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Accuracy of Information</h2>
    <p>
      We make reasonable efforts to ensure that the information on this Site is accurate and
      up to date. However, real estate law varies by state, county, and individual circumstance,
      and changes over time. We do not warrant that the information or documents generated by this
      Site are accurate, complete, or appropriate for any particular purpose or jurisdiction.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for verifying that any deed generated by this Site meets the requirements
      of the county recorder's office where you intend to file it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
    <p>
      THE SITE AND ALL SERVICES ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
      IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
      PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SITE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED,
      ERROR-FREE, OR FREE OF VIRUSES OR OTHER HARMFUL COMPONENTS.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WHATISAQUITCLAIMDEED.COM AND ITS OPERATORS SHALL
      NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES,
      OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS OR REVENUE, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OF THE SITE
      OR ANY DOCUMENTS GENERATED THROUGH THE SITE.
    </p>
    <p>
      IN NO EVENT SHALL OUR TOTAL LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ALL CLAIMS EXCEED ONE HUNDRED DOLLARS
      ($100.00).
    </p>

    <h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      The Site's design, code, content, and educational materials are the property of
      WhatIsAQuitclaimDeed.com and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.
      Deed documents generated by users through the Site are their own documents and are not
      subject to this restriction.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Your use of the Site is also subject to our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
      which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Modifications to Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. We will indicate the date of the
      last revision at the top of this page. Your continued use of the Site after any changes
      constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the United
      States, without regard to conflict of law principles.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms? <a href="/contact/">Contact us here.</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .breadcrumb {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--color-teal);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .page-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  ul {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-teal);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  a:hover {
    color: var(--color-teal-hover);
  }

  .notice-box {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-warning);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .notice-box p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .notice-box p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
